cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use the code or mathematical derivations in this repository, please
  cite the software using the metadata below. When referring to the scientific
  methods, model derivations, or research findings, also cite the associated
  PhD thesis listed under references.
title: "PhD-RUG – Spatially Adaptive Moment Models"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Verbiest
    given-names: Rik
    affiliation: University of Groningen
abstract: >-
  Research software and mathematical derivations developed as part of doctoral
  research on model-adaptive simulation of hierarchical moment models, with
  applications to shallow free-surface flows and rarefied gas dynamics. The
  repository includes Wolfram Mathematica notebooks for analytical derivations
  and reference simulations, along with Python software for simulating
  nonlinear moment models.
keywords:
  - adaptive moment models
  - model adaptivity
  - numerical simulation
  - shallow free-surface flows
  - rarefied gas dynamics
  - Wolfram Mathematica
  - Python
repository-code: "https://github.com/verbiestrik/PhD-RUG"
references:
  - type: thesis
    thesis-type: "Doctor of Philosophy"
    authors:
      - family-names: Verbiest
        given-names: Rik
    title: "Model-adaptive simulation of moment models with applications in shallow free-surface flows and rarefied gases"
    institution: University of Groningen
    publisher: University of Groningen
    location: Groningen, The Netherlands
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.33612/diss.1569659608"
    url: "https://research.rug.nl/en/publications/model-adaptive-simulation-of-moment-models-with-applications-in-s/"
    scope: >-
      Cite this thesis when referring to the scientific methods, model
      derivations, or research findings associated with the software.
    notes: "Award date: 26 October 2026."
